{"t": 1794109059.7677097, "kind": "call", "tool": "gitlab_create_merge_request_thread", "args": {"body": "**Root cause of the red `main` pipeline (pipeline 8812, commit a91c2e0)**\n\nThe `test:contract` job (job 77104) fails on the invoice-number contract:\n\n```\ncontract/test_invoice.py::test_invoice_number_format\nassert invoice_number(2026, 42) == \"INV-2026-000042\"\nE   AssertionError: assert 'INV-2026-42' == 'INV-2026-000042'\n```\n\n`billing/invoice.py` formatted the sequence with a plain `{seq}` placeholder, so the sequence part was not padded at all. The contract test (Finance ERP import, FIN-77) requires the sequence to be zero-padded to 6 digits.\n\n**Fix**\n\n```python\n# before\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq}\"\n\n# after\ndef invoice_number(year: int, seq: int) -> str:\n    return f\"INV-{year}-{seq:06d}\"\n```\n\nThis is a one-line change in `billing/invoice.py`: `seq` is now rendered as a zero-padded 6-digit field (`42` -> `000042`), while values that already have 6 digits (e.g. `123456`) are unchanged. I reproduced the contract test from the CI log locally against the patched module: 2 passed.\n\n**Note for this MR (erp-v2)**\n\nThis MR also reworks invoice numbering, so it will hit the same contract test. Please rebase on `main` and keep the 6-digit zero-padded sequence in the ERP v2 format, otherwise `test:contract` will fail on the MR pipeline as well. If ERP v2 is intended to change the sequence width or separators, that needs to be agreed with Finance and the `contract/test_invoice.py` expectations (FIN-77) updated in the same MR \u2014 it can't be changed on the service side alone.", "merge_request_iid": "12", "project_id": "acme/billing-legacy"}, "ok": true}
